nakama-daemon is a rewrite rather than a copy. It keeps the overall shape:
a daemon builder, subsystems with restart policies, cross-platform signal
handling, graceful shutdown with timeouts, a PID file, a single-instance
lock, metrics, IPC, and profiling. The implementation, error types, and
public API differ. This crate is distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 3 or later.
